# Driving the Minecraft Server

When the user asks for in-game actions (build something, op a player,
teleport, set time/weather, run a command), use this priority order.

## 1. Shared tool core — MCP and `/agent`

All in-world actions go through `agent/tools.py` (guardrailed RCON via
`docker exec mc-lan rcon-cli`). Two entry points use the same code:

- **Cursor**: `minecraft-builder` MCP (`mcp/minecraft_build_mcp.py`)
- **In-game**: `/agent <prompt>` → Paper plugin → host orchestrator → Ollama/cloud

Always prefer typed tools for in-world actions:

- Inspection: `server_status`, `preflight`, `list_players`,
  `get_player_position`, `get_player_dimension`
- Admin: `op_player`, `say`, `teleport_player`, `set_gamemode`, `set_time`,
  `set_weather`, `give_haste`, `backup_now`, `run_command` (escape hatch)
- Building: `fill_box`, `clear_box`, `build_platform`, `build_sphere`,
  `build_cylinder`, `build_spiral_staircase`
- FAWE: `fawe_as_player`, `fawe_sphere_at_player`, `mine_shaft_at_player`

### Guardrails (don't bypass without asking)

- `fill_box` / shape builders cap at **200,000** blocks
- generated commands cap at **20,000**
- Raw `run_command` is the escape hatch — prefer typed tools

### Bedrock vs Java names

Bedrock players show up via Floodgate with a leading `.`. When the user
says "lunar", confirm whether they mean `.LunarLicense582` (Bedrock) or a
Java handle. The dot is part of the name in commands.

## 2. Shell wrappers — for terminal work

When working from the host shell, use the project scripts instead of
hand-writing `docker exec`:

- `./mc.sh status | list | logs | console | backup`
- `./mc.sh op <name>` / `./mc.sh deop <name>`
- `./op.sh <name> [name...]` — bulk op
- `./mc.sh say "<message>"`
- `./mc.sh gamemode <mode> <player>`
- `./mc.sh cmd "<rcon command>"` — escape hatch

## 3. Raw `docker exec` — last resort

Only fall back to `docker exec -i mc-lan rcon-cli "<cmd>"` if neither MCP
nor the scripts can express what's needed.

## Building patterns

- Rectangular volumes → `fill_box` (`mode: replace|keep|hollow|outline`)
- Spheres / domes → `build_sphere` (`hollow: true` for shells)
- Towers / wells → `build_cylinder`
- Stairs → `build_spiral_staircase`
- Selections, copy/paste, `//regen`, brushes, schematics →
  `fawe_as_player` so the operation runs with that player's selection
- For absolute coordinates from console, vanilla `/fill` and `/setblock`
  via `run_command` is fine

Before any large or destructive op (clearing, replacing, regen), restate
the coordinates and approximate block count back to the user.
